Recover one evidence-grounded REPAIR contract: specify the reported trigger and each requested observable
outcome, without adding requirements the issue does not support.

The output is a behavioral contract for one evidence-backed precondition and observable postcondition. It is not
a description of the function's general intent, an implementation invariant, a root-cause analysis,
or a proposed fix. Do not add behavior merely because it seems desirable or conventional.

# Analysis checklist
Before authoring the obligation, reason through these questions:
1. What contract witness establishes the precondition before invocation?
2. Which evidence establishes the observed defect, and which evidence independently establishes intended behavior?
3. Is the required outcome a normal postcondition, an exceptional postcondition, or both?
   What is the weakest complete postcondition supported by the evidence, including every explicit variant that would expose a partial fix?
4. Can a witness reach the selected existing operation and observe the requested behavior, including behavior
   on an object constructed there when the requested method does not yet exist?
5. Is each support relation tied only to evidence supplied by the host?
6. If any required meaning lacks evidence, should this stage abstain instead of guessing?

The precondition and postcondition may cite different evidence. Include precondition evidence and
at least one normal_postcondition or exceptional_postcondition evidence item. Use normal_postcondition
only for successful return behavior. Use exceptional_postcondition for required or prohibited exceptions.
Always return both postcondition keys. Set the unused key to null; never omit either key.
For every returned REPAIR obligation, at least one of `normal_postcondition` or
`exceptional_postcondition` must be a non-empty string. Returning both as null is invalid. If no supported
postcondition can be stated, return no obligation and provide a non-empty `unsupported_reason` instead.
{% if packet.evidence_mode | default("canonical_spans") == "canonical_spans" %}
Select only `span_id` values supplied in `evidence_spans`. Span IDs are opaque references with no semantic
meaning; reason only from their attached text. Every evidence item must contain exactly `span_id` and `supports`.
The host owns quotation bytes, so do not reproduce evidence text inside an evidence item.
{% if prompt_profile == "contract-first-v3" %}
Represent the precondition as ordered atomic `precondition_clauses`. Each clause must state one independently
supportable setup or invocation fact and select every canonical `span_id` needed to support that fact. Include
the same span IDs as `precondition` evidence. Set the top-level `precondition` to the clause strings joined, in order,
with the literal separator ` AND `. Do not combine separately evidenced facts into one clause. Do not select
an unrelated span merely to satisfy the schema. At least one precondition clause must select issue evidence
that establishes the reported contract witness; generic API documentation alone is not the issue-specific
precondition. Qualification checks this mapping deterministically.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
Each quote must be copied as one exact contiguous verbatim span from the text under its evidence ID.
Never shorten a quote with `...`, join separate lines, or paraphrase inside the quote field.
{% endif %}
Do not propose a violation criterion; trusted host code derives it after grounding.
Do not describe a proposed patch. A repair_hypothesis is optional and diagnostic only.
{% if packet.include_rationales | default(false) %}
In rationale, explain the supporting context explicitly: identify the supplied precondition evidence and what it
establishes, identify the independent postcondition evidence and what it establishes, then explain why
their combination entails exactly the minimal caller-visible precondition and normal/exceptional postcondition fields. Do not use an
evidence ID as a substitute for describing the supporting text. Keep repair_hypothesis separate from this
evidence argument; the hypothesis is neither evidence nor contract authority.
{% else %}
The rationale field is optional and disabled for this run; omit it. Canonical evidence selections and
precondition-clause mappings remain mandatory and are validated by the host.
{% endif %}

Return an explicit unsupported_reason instead of inventing behavior.

