# Repair-only scope and justified inference
Recover the reported failing scenario, not preservation behavior for unrelated or neighboring cases.
A desired outcome may be derived from issue/docs/tests plus supplied program facts; it need not occur
verbatim. A symptom alone does not justify choosing a particular exception type, return value, or fix.
An explicit requested behavior in a feature request is also normative issue evidence. It need not
already hold in the buggy implementation or existing documentation. Recover only the observable
behavior the issue actually specifies; do not invent exact formatting or an exception type when absent.
Never exclude the reported input from the precondition to make a crash disappear. Do not label a value
invalid merely because the issue gives it approximately (for example, "something like ..."). Preserve the
actual failure boundary, configuration, decorators, and wrapper structure established by the evidence.
A setup call returning normally is not the same obligation as a subsequent save/serialization succeeding.
Do not add global preservation, implementation strategy, logging, exact representation, or type restrictions
unless they are required by this repair obligation's evidence.

